cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: >-
  Applicability-Aware Rule Retrieval for Regulation-Grounded
  Construction-Site Visual Screening
  — code, provision library and evaluation harness (ARGus)
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and evaluation harness for regulation-grounded visual
  compliance screening of construction sites. Given a site photograph, a bounded
  retrieval agent proposes the few provisions that plausibly apply, and the verdict
  is computed from a named provision formula over persisted checkpoint evidence
  rather than from model free text, so every decision traces back to a clause. The
  accompanying study reports where such pipelines fail: under the configurations
  tested it is the retrieval step -- deciding which provisions apply -- rather than
  the visual judgement that dominates end-to-end accuracy, and grounded precision
  decreased at every step as the candidate set was widened.
